From ec59db986891bb2b15bf2317b4d01e3aca495a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:14:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] mips: jz47xx: Add the Ingenic X2600 and the Flashforge
 Adventurer 5X

U-Boot proper only: the boot ROM's SPL (or Linux, for tests) has set up
the clocks and the DRAM before it runs. Console on UART0 (the DEBUG
header), the fractional baud registers reset so that plain 16550 divisors
from the 24 MHz EXCLK work. Timer: the global OST, a 64-bit counter at
24 MHz (the CP0 counter doesn't run). RAM: the 236 MiB of lowmem below
rmem and the RISC-V co-processor's region.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
